  "primary_scope_audit": [],
  "paired_qualitative_reflection": "Over EVERY commutative Q-algebra,let T be an arbitrary formal constant-coefficient operator with EXACTLY ZERO constant symbol coefficient,P any polynomial,and H monic of degree e>=1. Then qualitative all-marker eventual safety of(T,P) is EQUIVALENT to that of(T^e,H(P)),without a purity premise. The triangular A[t]-basis t^i H(t)^k,0<=i<e,has leading degree ek+i. Expansion into P^j proves forward safety;expansion in that basis and local nilpotence of T proves reflection using just the finite marker block Q,QP,...,QP^(e-1) for each original Q. Thus any fixed original bad Q gives at least one bad new block marker,degree<=degQ+D(e-1);not necessarily the same Q or every late index. Original purity implies new purity. Original purity is NOT reflected from new PURE tests alone. A unit leading coefficient is normalized by unit phase scaling;no nonunit-leading reflection or nonzero-constant-symbol theorem is asserted. All polynomial outputs and nilpotent coefficients are retained.",
  "all_ring_cutoffs_and_ordinary_ideals": "Under GVCRECOMPQUAL20261116,assume ORIGINAL purity and degP<=D>=1. An integer original cutoff C>=0 transfers to C_forward=ceil((CD+1)/e). An integer new cutoff C>=0 transfers back to C_backward=(1+eDC)(1+D(e-1)). Forward:expansion indices j>CdegQ vanish by original safety;the others have input degree<=(CD+1)degQ. Reverse:for basis indices i<e,k,terms with k>C(degQ+Di) vanish by the new cutoff;the remaining input degree is<=(1+eDC)(degQ+Di),giving the formula for positive marker degrees. Constants use ORIGINAL purity,which cannot be omitted. Thus linear-cutoff EXISTENCE is equivalent on the original pure locus over ALL Q-algebras. Literal ORDINARY ideals satisfy J(T^e,H(P)) subset J(T,P),I_Cforward(new) subset I_C(old),and I_Cbackward(old) subset J(old)+I_C(new). No radical replacement or infinite-ring ACC. For affine phases H(t)=t+c,every finite-prefix ordinary PURE ideal is EXACTLY unchanged by triangular induction;unit scaling is harmless. No same-index mixed-ideal equality or optimal cutoff is claimed.",
  "exact_height_slope_invariance": "Over EVERY characteristic-zero FIELD,for NONCONSTANT P and arbitrary formal T with lambda(0)0,define h_m=max{k:T^kP^m!=0},h_prime_m=max{k:T^kH(P)^m!=0},g_m=floor(h_prime_m/e),and M_N=max_(j<=N)h_j,with height0 at index0. No purity is needed for the exact asymptotic identity limsup h_m/m=limsup g_m/m. Expansion gives h_prime_m<=M_(em);the triangular phase-power basis and formal commutator lemma give M_N<=max_(k<=floor(N/e))h_prime_k+D(e-1). Running maxima of nonnegative at-most-linear sequences preserve limsup slope,and paired floor errors vanish. Consequently,on ORIGINAL purity,the exact asymptotic deficit gap liminf(m-h_m)/m is unchanged. Qualitative eventuality and linear-cutoff existence also agree,so a pure eventual-but-nonlinear obstruction is preserved and reflected under paired recomposition with original purity retained. For affine phases the entire running maximum sequence,and hence inf_m(m-h_m)/m,are exactly invariant. Individual heights need not be identified. This is a FIELD slope theorem,not an all-ring index assertion or a proof of the remaining gap alternative.",
